# Component Architecture & Code Quality
- **Component Size:** Prefer small, focused components over massive files.
- **Naming Convention:** Use `PascalCase` for component files (e.g., `HeroSection.jsx`).
- **File Structure:**
  - `src/components/layout/` - Headers, Footers, Navbars.
  - `src/components/ui/` - Shadcn UI/Radix primitives.
  - `src/pages/` - Full page assemblies.
- **Import Paths:** Use absolute aliased imports (e.g., `import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"`).
- **Cleanliness:** Remove unused imports, variables, and console logs before finalizing. Zero lint errors.
- **UI Primitives:** Shared responsive behavior belongs in `src/components/ui/`, `src/styles/globals.css`, or `tailwind.config.js` before being repeated across page components.
- **Custom Interaction Components:** App-specific reusable controls belong in `src/components/reui/` when they are not base shadcn/Radix primitives.
- **Page Shells:** Page-level components must account for safe areas, hidden scrollbars, and horizontal overflow protection.
- **Docs Sync:** UI architecture, screen behavior, route behavior, and design system changes must be documented in the matching `docs/` folder.
- **Backend Boundaries:** Keep secret-bearing integrations behind Express routes. Mapbox token/geocoding currently belongs in `backend/src/routes/mapboxRoutes.js` and `backend/src/controllers/mapboxController.js`.
- **Upload Boundaries:** File uploads must go through backend services. Do not upload from the frontend using provider secrets. Store provider-neutral metadata and keep Cloudinary `publicId` for future delete/migration behavior.
- **Firebase Admin Boundary:** Firebase Admin SDK belongs in the backend only. Seed Super Admin accounts through `backend/scripts/seedSuperAdmin.js`, never through public signup or frontend code.
- **Health Analytics Source:** Top illness or morbidity analytics must come from explicit case categories or consultation records. Never infer illness solely from medicine names or dispensing quantities.
- **Health Data Privacy:** Super Admin analytics should aggregate by barangay, health center, date bucket, and category by default. Patient-identifying case details require explicit authorization and audit logging.
